--TEST--
`Core\Request::queryAs<T>` and `postAs<T>` hydrate a declared class out of a parameter set, and answer what the same call over an inline shape answers — `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`, `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`
--GET--
q=novis&page=2
--POST--
name=ada&csrf=t0ken
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A written class and an inline shape are two spellings of one question at
// these members, so what a call is asked while compiling is the **owner's**
// answer and never the member's spelling: `queryAs` is written on a request
// here and on a database connection elsewhere, and only the second of those is
// asked `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`'s question about a column map.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Search {
    // `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`: a parameter set is a peer's
    // octets — `rule:security/tainted-sources` makes the query and the body
    // alike one — so the field that receives them is the field that declares
    // them.
    public tainted string $q;

    public function constructor(tainted string $q) {
        $this->q = $q;
    }
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Profile {
    public tainted string $name;

    public function constructor(tainted string $name) {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

var $search = Core\Request::queryAs<Search>();
echo $search->q, "\n";

var $profile = Core\Request::postAs<Profile>();
echo $profile->name, "\n";

// Agreement rather than two examples: the shape spelling of the same read
// answers the same thing, so a door that grew a rule of its own for one of the
// two targets fails here while still looking right on its own line.
echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Request::queryAs<tainted {q: string}>()), "\n";
--EXPECT--
novis
ada
{"q":"novis"}
